{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a5b0f2d975e98b549","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01NPSo7ed7WRJY4VssRY9uRG","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-7Kcibi/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-4nlDhF/8c82c996-e8ab-4c72-9ae0-43a5e7416901/tasks/a5b0f2d975e98b549.output","summary":"I read both files in full and compared every listed function statement-by-statement. Here is the result.\n\n## Findings\n\n**No behavioral discrepancies found.** Every function in the list is a faithful translation. Details below, plus a handful of non-behavioral deviations worth knowing about.\n\n### Function-by-function verdict (all faithful)\n\n| C | Rust | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|\n| `stbds_arrgrowf` (c 276-310) | rs 280-321 | Faithful. `min_len` uses `ptrdiff_t→size_t` conversion, `2*arrcap` in `size_t`, realloc size `elemsize*min_cap + 32`, `+32` re-base, `a==NULL` init of length/hash_table/temp, then unconditional `capacity=min_cap`. |\n| `stbds_arrfreef` (312-315) | 324-326 | Faithful (frees `a-32`, no null check, same as C). |\n| `stbds_rand_seed` (355-358) | 345-347 | Faithful. |\n| `stbds_hash_string` (477-491) | 520-536 | Faithful, including the two no-op `hash ^= hash ^ ROTATE_RIGHT(...)` idioms (which reduce to plain assignment in both), `(~hash)+(hash<<18)` using the pre-assignment `hash`, `*21`, `+= (hash<<6)`, final `+seed`. |\n| `stbds_siphash_bytes` (498-551) | 559-642 | Faithful — see sign-extension notes below. |\n| `stbds_hash_bytes` (553-556) | 645-647 | Faithful. |\n| `stbds_hmfree_func` (571-584) | 675-691 | Faithful. `a` is the raw array base in both; loop starts at `i=1`, re-reads `header(a)->length` each iteration, `strreset(&table->string)`, then frees `hash_table` then `header(a)`. |\n| `stbds_hmget_key_ts` (631-657) | 769-801 | Faithful, including the `length += 1` **before** `memset` ordering in the NULL branch, `*temp=-1` for the null-table case vs `STBDS_INDEX_EMPTY` for `slot<0`, and returning `a` (not `ARR_TO_HASH(a)`) in the else branch. |\n| `stbds_hmget_key` (659-665) | 804-815 | Faithful. |\n| `stbds_hmput_default` (667-676) | 818-836 | Faithful, including `length += 1` **before** `memset` (opposite of `hmput_key`). |\n| `stbds_hmput_key` (680-794) | 846-1030 | Faithful — see detailed notes below. |\n| `stbds_shmode_func` (796-805) | 1033-1041 | Faithful (`length = 1` assignment, not `+= 1`; `mode as u8` truncation). |\n| `stbds_hmdel_key` (807-868) | 1044-1132 | Faithful — see detailed notes below. |\n| `stbds_stralloc` (881-918) | 1146-1196 | Faithful. `512 << (block>>1)`, `++a->block` only when `blocksize < 1<<20`, oversized-block path splices behind `a->storage` without touching `remaining`, `sizeof(*sb)-8 == 8`. |\n| `stbds_strreset` (920-930) | 1199-1209 | Faithful (`memset` of 24 bytes). |\n| `strkey` (939-943) | 1219-1257 | Faithful; the hand-rolled `%d` formatter matches `printf(\"%d\")` for the whole `int` range including `INT_MIN`, and writes into a private 256-byte static. |\n| `arr_push` (945-956) | 1260-1291 | Faithful expansion of `arrmaybegrow`/`arrput`/`arrfree` with `elemsize == 4`, `i += 50` outer step. |\n| `stbds_make_hash_index` (385-472) | 371-503 | Faithful — see notes. |\n| `stbds_probe_position` (367-373) | 357-359 | Faithful. |\n| `stbds_log2` (375-383) | 361-369 | Faithful. |\n| `stbds_is_key_equal` (558-564) | 653-672 | Faithful (`mode >= STBDS_HM_STRING` → strcmp on `*(char**)(a+elemsize*i+keyoffset)`, else memcmp of `keysize`). |\n| `stbds_hm_find_slot` (586-629) | 693-766 | Faithful, both probe sub-loops, `hash<2 → hash+=2` before `probe_position`, `(pos & ~7)+i` return. |\n| `stbds_strdup` (870-876) | 838-843 | Faithful. |\n| Macros `stbds_header`/`temp`/`temp_key`/`arrlen`/`arrcap`/`HASH_TO_ARR`/`ARR_TO_HASH`/`ALIGN_FWD`/`ROTATE_LEFT`/`ROTATE_RIGHT`/`load_32_or_64` | 213-273, 353-359, 510-517, 412-433 | All faithful. |\n\n### Specifically verified high-risk items\n\n**Sign extension in `stbds_siphash_bytes`.** All four sites are correct:\n- Main loop low word (c 523 / rs 578-582): C's `d[0]|(d[1]<<8)|(d[2]<<16)|(d[3]<<24)` is `int`-typed and sign-extends into `size_t`. Rust builds a `u32` then `((lo as i32) as isize) as usize` — exact match.\n- Main loop high word (c 524 / rs 583-587): the C cast `(size_t)(...)` happens **before** `<<16<<16`, so the sign-extended 64-bit value is shifted. Rust does `((((hi as i32) as isize) as usize) << 16) << 16` — cast-then-shift order preserved.\n- Tail `case 4` (c 536 / rs 614): `(d[3] << 24)` sign-extends. Rust `((*d.add(3) as i32).wrapping_shl(24)) as isize as usize` — correct.\n- Tail `cases 3/2/1` (c 537-539 / rs 617-623): values stay positive; Rust routes them through `i32 → isize → usize` which is a no-op. Correct.\n\n**Switch fall-through in the siphash tail** (c 532-541 / rs 602-625): the C `switch(len-i)` with no `break`s is rendered as a cascade of `if rem >= 7 { } if rem >= 6 { } …`, which reproduces the fall-through exactly for every `rem` in 0..=7. `case 0: break` maps to no work. `data = len << 56` is set before the cascade in both.\n\n**`stbds_temp_key` asymmetry in `stbds_hmput_key`.** Confirmed present in the Rust: the first inner probe loop (c 731-734 / rs 924-933) sets `stbds_temp(a)` **and**, when `mode >= STBDS_HM_STRING`, `stbds_temp_key(a) = *(char**)(raw_a + elemsize*index + keyoffset)`; the second inner loop (c 749-750 / rs 961-962) sets only `stbds_temp(a)`. The asymmetry is copied.\n\n**`a` vs `raw_a` usage.** In `stbds_hmput_key` the C reuses the names confusingly (`raw_a` holds the *hash* pointer, `a` the raw base after line 694). The Rust reproduces this exactly at rs 866-867, and every downstream use matches: `stbds_is_key_equal(raw_a, …)` (c 730/748 → rs 915/952), `temp_key` source from `raw_a` (c 733 → rs 926-931), `stbds_temp(a)`/`header(a)->length`/element writes from `a` (c 731/779/786-789 → rs 924/996/1002), returns `STBDS_ARR_TO_HASH(a,elemsize)`. In `stbds_hmdel_key` the 