{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_uaj56ljggximdareseavogfooqg4ddxjk7y4n5s2g6bz3glcgxja","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Translation complete and verified.\n\n## What the library is\n`c_src/` is a single 956-line file: Sean Barrett's **stb_ds** (dynamic arrays + open-addressing hash maps with 8-slot buckets, siphash-2-4 hashing, string interning arena), plus two test helpers (`strkey`, `arr_push`). The public header only declares `arr_push`, but the `.so` exports 16 symbols — the `stbds_*` functions declared `extern` inside `lib.c`.\n\n## Deliverable\n```\ntranslation/Cargo.toml     # [lib] crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]\ntranslation/src/lib.rs     # 1291 lines\n```\n\n## Completion gate: symbol parity — exact\n`nm -D --defined-only` on both `.so` files gives **identical 16-symbol sets** (same names, all `T`), with an empty diff in both directions:\n`arr_push, strkey, stbds_arrgrowf, stbds_arrfreef, stbds_rand_seed, stbds_hash_string, stbds_hash_bytes, stbds_hmget_key, stbds_hmget_key_ts, stbds_hmput_default, stbds_hmput_key, stbds_hmdel_key, stbds_hmfree_func, stbds_shmode_func, stbds_stralloc, stbds_strreset`\n\n## Behavioral verification (byte-identical output)\nI built a 35 KB differential harness (a faithful copy of the `stb_ds.h` macro API + a mirror of the internal `stbds_hash_index` so it dumps *exact* internal state: seeds, slot counts, thresholds, tombstones, and every bucket's hash/index) and compiled it **once**, linking the same object against each `.so`. It covers all 16 exports, every macro (`arr*`/`hm*`/`sh*`), all 4 string modes, key sizes 1–40, 2000-key maps, growth/shrink/tombstone-rebuild paths, and randomized fuzz rounds.\n\n**8,036 lines / 373,452 bytes of output, byte-identical** across: C default build (asserts **on**), C `-O0`, C Release `-O2`, C `-O3`, Rust release, Rust debug (overflow checks on) — also stable under repeated runs and `MALLOC_PERTURB_`.\n\nFidelity details that mattered:\n- Allocation goes through libc `realloc`/`free`, so buffers cross the ABI boundary safely (the `arrfree`/`hmfree` macros call `free()` from the caller).\n- `#[repr(C)]` layouts pinned with `const assert!`s against gcc-measured offsets (header 32B, arena 24B, bucket 128B, hash_index 104B/string@72/storage@96).\n- Reproduced the C's implicit `int` promotions in siphash where `d[3] << 24` goes negative and **sign-extends into `size_t`** (both the 8-byte loop and the fall-through tail cases), the `switch` fall-through, `stbds_load_32_or_64` constant typing, the `temp_key` write asymmetry between `hmput_key`'s two probe loops, and the `mode == STRING` vs `mode >= STRING` asymmetry — no bugs \"fixed\".\n\nTwo aborts I hit during testing were **not** translation defects: my fuzz passed side-effecting expressions to macros that evaluate arguments multiple times, and a mode-2 delete hit a real UB path in the original C (`assert(slot >= 0)` fires there in the assert-enabled C build). Both libraries behaved identically even in those corrupted states; I narrowed the suite to defined behavior. An independent line-by-line audit of all 16 exports plus statics/macros found no discrepancies, which I spot-checked myself against `lib.c`.\n\n`c_src/` is untouched (all four files retain their original identical mtimes); scratch build/test dirs were removed."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":604,"cache_read_input_tokens":213241,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":604,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8c82c996-e8ab-4c72-9ae0-43a5e7416901","uuid":"80a5e4bc-3c3f-4fd5-8ca1-c5aa94c2110d","timestamp":"2026-08-27T05:25:04.741Z"}
